    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- `HasMyProp myLT`</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">discr_tree_key</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HasMyProp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myLT</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- `HasMyProp (@LT.lt myNat _)`</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">discr_tree_key</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HasMyProp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 590910830,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1777153817
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What does that tell me?</p>",
        "id": 590911021,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1777154057
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I believe all the instances are filtered based on the key (it's used to search among all of them), and since the key differs that explains why the instance wasn't even attempted.<br>\nBut then the question becomes why is the key different? I thought it's usually the head term only</p>",
        "id": 590911765,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777154757
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>All this now looks expected, given the data above. What are you asking exactly?</p>\n<p><code>&lt;</code> is notation for <code>LT.lt</code>.</p>\n<p>Actually maybe I'm a bit confused because they're equal with <code>reducible_and_instances</code>.</p>",
        "id": 590913434,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1777156060
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>discr tree happens at reducible transparency, not reducible and instances</p>",
        "id": 590913697,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1777156316
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Typeclass.20synthesis.20fails.20with.20.28.C2.B7.20.3C.20.C2.B7.29/near/590911765\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>But then the question becomes why is the key different? I thought it's usually the head term only</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>usually instances in mathlib which only index the head term will have <code>(priority := 100)</code> and <code>-- see note [reduced instance priority]</code></p>",
        "id": 590913939,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1777156523
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Typeclass.20synthesis.20fails.20with.20.28.C2.B7.20.3C.20.C2.B7.29/near/590913939\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Typeclass.20synthesis.20fails.20with.20.28.C2.B7.20.3C.20.C2.B7.29/near/590911765\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>But then the question becomes why is the key different? I thought it's usually the head term only</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>usually instances in mathlib which only index the head term will have <code>(priority := 100)</code> and <code>-- see note [reduced instance priority]</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Well this is an observation of what people do when they notice this, we can't choose the disctree ourselves can we?</p>",
        "id": 590915916,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1777158690
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Morally i think the above should be in scope for instance synthesis to find, but i have seen no documentation suggesting either way.<br>\n(Of course one can argue that the current implementation is exactly what is in scope...)</p>",
